Title:
CrystalPotato – GodPotato in Crystal

Type:
Blog Post

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- Write-up and release notes for CrystalPotato, a Crystal-language port of GodPotato that performs Windows local privilege escalation from accounts with `SeImpersonatePrivilege` to `NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM`.  
- It abuses the DCOM OXID Resolver by hooking an RPC dispatch entry in `combase.dll`, coercing the SYSTEM OXID Resolver to authenticate to an attacker-controlled named pipe, then impersonating and duplicating a SYSTEM token to spawn a SYSTEM process.  
- The post emphasizes reducing .NET-related forensic and reverse-engineering artifacts by producing a native PE with fewer obvious strings/metadata.  
- It adds OPSEC hardening: indirect syscalls with SSN resolution via ntdll’s Exception Directory, dynamic Win32 API resolution via PEB/export parsing with DJB2 hashes, compile-time XOR string obfuscation, and RTTI name sanitization.  
- Useful for red teams, pentesters, and offensive tool developers targeting service contexts (IIS app pools, MSSQL, Network/Local Service) where `SeImpersonatePrivilege` is present.  
- Interesting because it combines a widely reliable LPE chain (GodPotato) with multiple anti-signature/anti-telemetry implementation choices in a less common language (Crystal).

Technical Focus:
- DCOM OXID Resolver coercion + RPC dispatch table hooking in `combase.dll`
- Named pipe impersonation (`ImpersonateNamedPipeClient`) and token duplication/spawn (`CreateProcessAsUserW` / `CreateProcessWithTokenW`)
- In-process COM marshaling/unmarshaling with crafted `OBJREF` over `ncacn_ip_tcp`
- Indirect syscalls with SSN resolution via ntdll Exception Directory + stub trampoline into ntdll `.text`
- PEB walking + export table parsing for dynamic API resolution (DJB2 hashing)
- Compile-time string obfuscation and metadata/RTTI minimization

Use Cases:
- Escalate from IIS/MSSQL/Service accounts with `SeImpersonatePrivilege` to SYSTEM
- Post-exploitation privilege escalation on Windows 10/11 and Server editions
- Execute SYSTEM commands, obtain a SYSTEM reverse shell, or create a local admin user
- Develop/experiment with Crystal-based offensive tooling and OPSEC tradeoffs
- Study/replicate GodPotato-style DCOM/RPC coercion and token theft chains

Keywords:
Crystal language, GodPotato, local privilege escalation, SeImpersonatePrivilege, DCOM, OXID Resolver, combase.dll, RPC dispatch table hook, UseProtseq, named pipe impersonation, ImpersonateNamedPipeClient, OBJREF, COM marshaling, ncacn_ip_tcp, token duplication, CreateProcessAsUserW, CreateProcessWithTokenW, indirect syscalls, SSN resolution, ntdll Exception Directory, PEB walking, export table parsing, DJB2 hashing, string obfuscation, RTTI sanitization